## Original Content
Au Kenya, un jeune créateur de mode mise sur des vêtements entièrement réalisés à la main pour se démarquer. Il utilise exclusivement des métiers à tisser manuels afin de préserver et de remettre au goût du jour des savoir-faire traditionnels menacés par l'industrialisation. Récit de Laurent Berstecher.

## Summary
A young fashion designer in Kenya is using manual looms to create handmade clothing and revive traditional weaving techniques threatened by industrialization. This initiative aims to preserve cultural heritage by making traditional craftsmanship fashionable again.

## Key Points
- A Kenyan fashion designer exclusively uses manual looms for handmade clothing to stand out.
- Traditional weaving skills are at risk due to industrialization.
- The designer aims to preserve and popularize these endangered crafts.
- The project highlights the importance of safeguarding cultural heritage.
- The story is narrated by journalist Laurent Berstecher.


